  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>Staying in Bandol</h2>
      <p>This page brings together what official sources say about Bandol for anyone staying there with a dog. It does not name a specific hotel or campsite: no source read lists the accommodation in town that accepts dogs, and each sets its own conditions (supplement, size, number of dogs, rooms concerned). Ask them directly before booking.</p>
      <h2>The Dog Beach</h2>
      <p>The town of Bandol and its tourist office state that one beach is dedicated to dogs: the Dog Beach, below the Deferrari stadium, Corniche Bonaparte, with a view of the island of Bendor. According to the town, eight beaches are open to the public all year. The sources read do not give the rule for the other beaches: ask the town hall before taking your dog there.</p>
      <h2>Walks and outings</h2>
      <p>According to the tourist office, a leash is required on the trails, including the coastal path and the Bandol Classic; access to the hills may be closed during heatwaves, high winds or fire risk (check before you set off). For a short outing, the tourist office mentions the Parc du Canet (the town's largest park), the lawns of the Plage Centrale, the Square Haffner and the Parc du Bois Maurin. A dog water fountain stands in front of the tourist office (3 allées Alfred Vivien), and "Toutounet" bag dispensers are spread around town. The tourist office adds that most shops and restaurants accept dogs on a leash on their terraces; this is not a guarantee for every establishment.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the tourist office advises walking early in the morning or late in the day in summer, and checking your dog's ears after a walk (grass seeds).</div>
      <h2>Check before booking</h2>
      <p>Dog policy, supplement and restrictions: to confirm with each hotel or campsite. Sources: Bandol tourist office (Dog Beach page and "Holidays in Bandol with a dog" article), town of Bandol (Beaches page), read on 12/11/2026.</p>
